            {
                "entry_id": "0e357fdc-e616-321f-bbb1-16836e80f616",
                "word": "fane",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5dfebc3c-2fe9-4ca2-889a-8552d2e05291",
                        "entry_id": "0e357fdc-e616-321f-bbb1-16836e80f616",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "fanes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f6e86286-bafd-3b9a-a0f7-93653e621142",
                        "entry_id": "0e357fdc-e616-321f-bbb1-16836e80f616",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A temple or sacred place."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "15ac350b-6bb2-48d2-bf41-6f7ade05472e",
                                "sense_id": "f6e86286-bafd-3b9a-a0f7-93653e621142",
                                "text": "And Pallas rear'd him; her ovvn unctuous fane / She made his habitation, vvhere vvith bulls / The youth of Athens, and vvith ſlaughter'd lambs / Her annual vvorſhip celebrate."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "37c4dc25-e723-43bb-953d-7f50190ddd5d",
                                "sense_id": "f6e86286-bafd-3b9a-a0f7-93653e621142",
                                "text": "Crown me, therefore,—and minstrelling near to thy fanes, Bacchus, thickly-adorned with rosy chaplets will I dance with a full-bosomed maid."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5bed8308-9855-44ff-945b-360b9c8a1fea",
                                "sense_id": "f6e86286-bafd-3b9a-a0f7-93653e621142",
                                "text": "Indeed, the bells were tolling, the people were trooping into the handsome church, the carriages of the inhabitants of the lordly quarter poured forth their pretty loads of devotees, in whose company Pen and his uncle, ending their edifying conversation, entered the fane."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb4ec709-2b14-47e8-975c-4d4074a40495",
                                "sense_id": "f6e86286-bafd-3b9a-a0f7-93653e621142",
                                "text": "Fanes are built around it for a distance of 3, 4 or 5 Indian miles; but whether these are Jaina, or more strictly Hindu is not mentioned."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31b9945d-8a27-4b48-8fa0-d48e61e79862",
                                "sense_id": "f6e86286-bafd-3b9a-a0f7-93653e621142",
                                "text": "The priests of the Germans and Britons were druids. They had their sacred oaken groves. Such were their steeple houses. Nature was to some extent a fane to them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5ffe42b-1be0-4e2e-90bc-ef5795a8aff1",
                                "sense_id": "f6e86286-bafd-3b9a-a0f7-93653e621142",
                                "text": "It was a wonderful sight to see the full moon looking down on the ruined fane of Kør."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5c5ded5-834b-4196-abf9-d2e1589f5286",
                                "sense_id": "f6e86286-bafd-3b9a-a0f7-93653e621142",
                                "text": "And this ideal conception is found beaming like a golden ray upon each idol, however coarse and grotesque, in the crowded galleries of the sombre fanes of India and other Mother lands of cults."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "307ee5d6-3cd2-44b6-b865-c21f59ac5b7e",
                                "sense_id": "f6e86286-bafd-3b9a-a0f7-93653e621142",
                                "text": "He was thinking; but the glory of the song, the swell from the great organ, the clustered lights, […] the height and vastness of this noble fane, its antiquity and its strength—all these things seemed to have their part as causes of the thrilling emotion that accompanied his thoughts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ff9bb8e-fe8c-46c6-8cc6-2c9c594b3430",
                                "sense_id": "f6e86286-bafd-3b9a-a0f7-93653e621142",
                                "text": "[The bookshop] seemed like a secret fane, some shrine of curious rites, and the young man's throat was tightened by a stricture which was half agitation and half tobacco."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "1d5fa0a8-8c7a-38ee-a417-e844932663d8",
                "word": "fane",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "01f920b6-65de-42e5-974d-36f6e79f92ac",
                        "entry_id": "1d5fa0a8-8c7a-38ee-a417-e844932663d8",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "fanes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c4239311-c6be-3471-a917-090769459a95",
                        "entry_id": "1d5fa0a8-8c7a-38ee-a417-e844932663d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A weathercock, a weather vane."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2d8b9aae-d045-449e-a471-79e9306dd0a4",
                                "sense_id": "c4239311-c6be-3471-a917-090769459a95",
                                "text": "The ſteeple had become old and ruinous; and therefore the preſent one was built about the year 1740. It had, at that time, four fanes mounted on ſpires, on the four corners; theſe being judged too weak for the fanes, were taken down in 1764, and the roof of the ſteeple altered."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9102b9ff-d7bb-30e4-a5e1-5cf1eb5adbff",
                        "entry_id": "1d5fa0a8-8c7a-38ee-a417-e844932663d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A banner, especially a military banner."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5fa3ae3a-2f8e-49cb-959b-b623f93e4b46",
                                "sense_id": "9102b9ff-d7bb-30e4-a5e1-5cf1eb5adbff",
                                "text": "So fate fell-woven forward drave him,\nand with malice Mordred his mind hardened,\nsaying that war was wisdom and waiting folly.\n‘Let their fanes be felled and their fast places\nbare and broken, burned their havens,\nand isles immune from march of arms\nor Roman reign now reek to heaven\nin fires of vengeance! [I.18-25]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
